      "side": 1,
      "message": "Eviction doesn\u0027t depend on apply time: Immediate and OnReset both call requestActivation() synchronously, and Activation::activation(Activating) -\u003e freeSpace() -\u003e ItemUpdater::erase() removes an older version\u0027s entry from updateManagers. If StartUpdate was invoked on that version\u0027s Update object (e.g. second update via the version returned by the first), its Manager is destroyed while processImage() is still running. Reproduced on QEMU evb-ast2600: the daemon aborts with \"corrupted size vs. prev_size\" without the fix.\n\nAgreed that the flag must not be cleared early. It is now cleared after requestActivation() returns, as before, through a shared_ptr\u003cbool\u003e copy so the write is safe if the Manager was destroyed. Re-tested: both updates reach Active, NRestarts\u003d0.",
